<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= lang %>" data-theme="<%= theme.followingSystem ? 'system' : theme.id %>">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title><%= strings.pageTitle %></title>
    <%# The conversation and analysis styles, which this page alone uses. %>
    <%- include('partials/theme-head', { pageStyles: ['questionnaire'] }) %>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
    <header>
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow"><%= strings.subtitle %></p>
            <h1><%= strings.heading %></h1>
        </div>
        <div class="switchers">
            <%# THE PICKER STAYS HERE RATHER THAN MOVING TO A MENU BAR, because this page has
                no menu bar: it is the participant's questionnaire, not a console view, and it
                carries no navigation between console pages. The console's picker moved into
                `console-nav.ejs`, which is shared by the three views that have one. %>
            <%- include('partials/theme-picker') %>
            <div class="lang-switch">
                <% supportedLangs.forEach(function (code, i) { %><% if (i > 0) { %>·<% } %><a href="?lang=<%= code %>" class="<%= code === lang ? 'active' : '' %>"><%= code.toUpperCase() %></a><% }); %>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>
    <p class="intro"><%= strings.intro %></p>

    <div class="card">
        <%#
            THE TOKEN IS THE ONLY WAY IN, so there is no access-code prompt and no
            start button. This page is rendered only for a token that resolved (see
            renderQuestionnaire in lib/auth/participant-routes.js, its single caller),
            so the conversation is never hidden and the client starts it directly.

            A tokenless "unlock" form used to sit here, guarded by `if (!tokenResolved)`.
            That branch could not be reached: every caller passed tokenResolved: true,
            so the markup was dead and the field asked for a shared code that no route
            anywhere accepted. Both the field and the code are gone. See the note on
            mayUseQuestionnaire in lib/routes-api.js.
        %>
        <div id="conversation">
            <div id="history" class="history"></div>
            <div id="input-area" class="row">
                <input type="text" id="input" placeholder="<%= strings.inputPlaceholder %>">
                <button id="send-btn">&#10148;</button>
            </div>
            <div id="actions" class="actions hidden">
                <%#
                    HIDDEN FOR THE PoC, at the owner's request: "the button of download markdown
                    can be hidden for now as it is not really useful". Hidden rather than deleted
                    so it is one attribute away from coming back - the handler, the string and
                    the styling all stay.

                    THE LISTENER IS GUARDED IN audit.js, which is what makes this safe: it used
                    to bind `$('download-md')` unconditionally, so an absent button threw and
                    took the rest of the listener block with it. See the note there.
                %>
                <button id="download-md" class="secondary" hidden><%= strings.downloadMarkdown %></button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="analysis" class="card hidden">
        <h2 id="analysis-heading"><%= strings.analysisTitle %></h2>
        <div id="analysis-body"></div>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    window.AUDIT_CONFIG = {
        toolId: "<%= toolId %>",
        lang: "<%= lang %>",
        // The base path, so client-side fetch() builds the same URLs the server
        // serves under. Empty when the app is at the root.
        basePath: "<%= basePath %>",
        // The participant's link token, so an answer is attributed to them. It is
        // already in the page URL, so exposing it here reveals nothing new, and
        // without it answers could not be attached to a participant.
        participantToken: <%- JSON.stringify(typeof participantToken === 'string' ? participantToken : null) %>,
        // Work already done, so a returning participant resumes rather than
        // starting again. This is what a reset preserves.
        existingResponses: <%- JSON.stringify(typeof existingResponses === 'undefined' ? [] : existingResponses) %>,
        strings: <%- JSON.stringify(strings) %>
    };
</script>
<script src="<%= basePath %>/js/audit.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
